## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates expertise in real-time blind source separation for production telemetry systems, combining theoretical signal processing with practical systems engineering under edge computing constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Online ICA and whitening for streaming data processing
- Adaptive forgetting mechanisms for nonstationary source tracking
- Temporal permutation resolution across sliding windows
- Edge infrastructure latency and computational optimization
- Validation methodology using synthetic ground-truth injection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Online Infomax-like ICA implementation
function onlineICA(whitenedData, learningRate) {
  // Initialize separation matrix
  let W = initializeMatrix();

  return function update(newSample) {
    // Natural gradient update
    const y = W * newSample;
    const g = tanh(y);
    const delta = learningRate * (g * newSample - (1 - g * g) * W);

    // Update separation matrix
    W += delta;
    return y;
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This scenario introduces motion-induced Doppler effects and wind noise, creating a practical non-stationary blind source separation problem. It tests understanding of online adaptation, cross-bin permutation alignment, and evaluation without perfect ground truth.

## Key Concepts
- Convolutive ICA in the STFT domain with online whitening
- Per-bin ICA versus joint diagonalization: latency versus frequency coherence trade-offs
- Cross-bin permutation using magnitude consistency and phase continuity cues
- Lightweight on-device evaluation using surrogate ground-truth signals

## Code Example
```javascript
function onlineWhiten(x, forgetFactor, state) {
  const alpha = forgetFactor;
  state.mean = alpha * state.mean + (1 - alpha) * x;
  state.cov = alpha * state.cov + (1 - alpha) * (x - state.mean).outer(x - state.mean);
  const whitened = (x - state.mean) * inv(sqrt(eigenvalues(state.cov)));
  return whitened;
}
```

